welcome back vaccine eligibility is  expanding here in nevada starting next  week  on monday anyone 16 and older will be  eligible to receive the covet 19 vaccine  and this morning senators jackie rosen  and catherine cortez-masto made a visit  to a major vaccination site here in las  vegas our bianca holman reports  moderna pfizer and johnson and johnson  kova 19 vaccines are all given here at  the cashman center  it's an example of the coordinated  effort between federal  state and local authorities senators  rosen and cortez masto got a look inside  at the site  escorted by leaders from the health  district fire department and fema  those who were vaccinated in the  observation section listened to the  henderson symphony  and spoke with the senators people  shared their good and bad moments during  the pandemic  one woman experiencing job loss and a  first-time father  raising a baby these senators say  vaccines are essential not only to save  lives but also to get our economy  back on track this site is proof  to our travelers that want to come back  to las vegas that we want  those over what 50 million visitors that  we're safe and we can do this safely  we can do it safely here we can work  with our properties we can work with our  businesses  to really make sure people feel  comfortable and safe the vaccine is free  of charge but you must make an  appointment  our state's timeline to make the vaccine  available to all adults is in line and  ahead of president joe biden's challenge  to have vaccines available for all  adults by may 1st  and you can make an appointment to  receive the covet 19 vaccine on the  southern nevada health district's  website  bialcoholman 8 news now
 

